<p>Cuba said on March 12 it will release 51 people from prison in the coming days under an agreement brokered with the Vatican — a move widely described as unexpected. The announcement comes as the government faces growing pressure from the United States, including from the Trump administration. Rights advocates say it is still unclear whether political prisoners will be among those freed, and many political detainees remain behind bars.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/G6GMgk8GSvxZpYjafFRjqaFUFghH5AngA6i-NrR_qEs3vMU5DqwgdhI1IHE0Sz-yXxNfGcZ4uA59tK_H3SSLlpIpccth8GWJwM8pvwDq4v75PVf6HZ2NFdsRO6H5VTjRiqRVYn5wErNgCasWdy2SHEUuSRPk20HmV-2qme63Iks3hl1cW6P38vzVKKuG-UPBWyXWiJ-_IFjhcQ' alt='The Capitol building in Havana.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Selection criteria: A Cuban official said those slated for release have served most of their sentences and shown good conduct.</li><li>Political detainees: Rights groups cited by DW say more than 1,200 political detainees remain in Cuban jails; it is still unclear whether any are among those set to be freed.</li><li>Oil supplies: The New York Times reported the Trump administration has tried to squeeze Havana by restricting oil supplies in what it described as an oil blockade.</li><li>Broader context: Straits Times said the planned releases come as Washington presses Cuba to reform its one-party rule.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Cuban government: Officials said the releases will go ahead under an agreement reached after talks involving the Holy See. (<a href='https://www.indopremier.com/ipotnews/newsDetail.php?jdl=Cuba_announces_release_of_51_prisoners_after_talks_with_Vatican__official&amp;news_id=1723448&amp;group_news=ALLNEWS&amp;taging_subtype=CUBA&amp;name=&amp;search=y_general&amp;q=CUBA,%20&amp;halaman=1'>IndoPremier</a>)</li><li>Human rights groups: Advocates cited in reporting said it remains unclear whether political prisoners are included among those set to be freed. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/cuba-to-release-51-prisoners-after-talks-with-vatican/a-76340936'>DW</a>)</li><li>Trump administration (US): Reporting portrayed the releases as an attempt to ease tensions with Washington as the administration ramps up pressure on Havana. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/12/world/americas/cuba-prisoner-release-trump-oil-blocade.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/cuba-to-release-51-prisoners-under-agreement-with-the-vatican'>Cuba to release 51 prisoners in Vatican-brokered deal</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/cuba-to-release-51-prisoners-after-talks-with-vatican/a-76340936'>Cuba to release 51 prisoners after talks with Vatican</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/12/world/americas/cuba-prisoner-release-trump-oil-blocade.html'>Cuba Pledges to Release 51 Prisoners Amid U.S. Pressure</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/cuba-51-jail-releases-trump/'>Cuba to release 51 people from prison in surprise move amid Trump pressure</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/cuba-release-51-people-prison-unexpected-move-131022776'>Cuba will release 51 people from prison in an unexpected move</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.indopremier.com/ipotnews/newsDetail.php?jdl=Cuba_announces_release_of_51_prisoners_after_talks_with_Vatican__official&amp;news_id=1723448&amp;group_news=ALLNEWS&amp;taging_subtype=CUBA&amp;name=&amp;search=y_general&amp;q=CUBA,%20&amp;halaman=1'>Cuba announces plans to release 51 prisoners following discussions with the Holy See, stating that the detainees have served most of their sentences and demonstrated good conduct.</a> - indopremier.com</li></ul>